diff --git a/docs/architecture.md b/docs/architecture.md
index b0263fb..2fc4554 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -171,7 +171,7 @@ All of these live in `native_x_renderer/` and contain no game-specific code.
 | Command queue | Each call captured on the game's render thread into a command (the tracker's record of register changes (D73), programs, surfaces, arguments, an inline draw's data), run in order by NativeXRenderer's own thread; 4096 commands; the command processor waits for it before every signal to the game (D71). `native_x_renderer_thread` off: run on capture. | SDK `SetSignalGate` (the SDK's `recomp` change 31) |
 | Shader cache | Microcode copied at load, hashed and analyzed on the render thread; SPIR-V from the SDK's `SpirvShaderTranslator` and the Diligent shader object, per modification, made on two worker threads with a translator each (D34). A draw whose shaders are not ready is skipped. | SDK translator |
 | Pipeline cache | Pipelines keyed by shader pair, primitive type, render target formats, MSAA, blend/depth/stencil/raster state. Compiled in DiligentCore's thread pool (D28), with DiligentCore's (Vulkan's) pipeline cache; a draw whose pipeline is not ready is skipped. A pipeline not drawn for 600 frames lets go of its textures: its bindings would keep alive textures the texture cache evicted or the resolve registry freed (D55). | DiligentCore |
-| Shader cache file | One indexed file: the shaders, translations (SPIR-V) and pipelines a game used, and the Vulkan pipeline cache; prepared before the game draws, with a status for its screen (D42, D45, D52, D115, `src/storage.cpp`). | — |
+| Shader cache file | One indexed file: the shaders, translations (SPIR-V) and pipelines a game used, and the Vulkan pipeline cache; prepared before the game draws, with a status for its screen (D42, D45, D52, D127, `src/storage.cpp`). | — |
 | Guest memory mirror | The GPU-side copy of guest memory that the translated shaders fetch vertices from and indexed draws take indices from, kept current page by page for the ranges draws use. Indices are swapped by the vertex shader. A page invalidated by a CPU write is copied again only if its data hash changed (D35): the invalidation is coarser than the writes. The SDK's range requests keep their merged ranges between calls (D84, the SDK's `recomp` change 32). | SDK `SharedMemory` on a Diligent buffer (D17) |
 | Primitive processing | Host primitive and vertex shader types, index conversions. | SDK `PrimitiveProcessor` (D17) |
 | Texture cache | Host textures from fetch constants: address, format, size, tiling, mips, loaded by the SDK's load shaders as DiligentCore compute pipelines. Block formats (DXT1 to DXN) stay compressed on the host when their size is a multiple of the block (D33). Invalidated when the CPU writes their pages (the mirror's page watches); an outdated texture whose guest data hashes the same is not loaded again. Each texture reports its host size, mips included, to the SDK's memory limits. | SDK `TextureCache` on DiligentCore textures (D23) |
